From: qdistro <qdistro@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] include: install xwayland-api.h from the libweston headers

Reproducible record of the in-place edit to
src/include/libweston/meson.build (see libweston-vendored/README.md: the
patches are the record, the tree is already patched).

Upstream weston installs include/libweston/xwayland-api.h from
compositor/meson.build, part of the weston *frontend*. This vendored tree
builds libweston only and omits the compositor/ subdir, so the header --
declared as `xwayland_api_h` in include/libweston/meson.build but consumed
nowhere -- was never installed into the prefix.

qdwin/qdwin.c includes <libweston/xwayland-api.h> unconditionally and calls
weston_xwayland_surface_get_api() to tag XWayland toplevels
(qdwin_toplevel_is_xwayland). Building qdwin against the vendored prefix
therefore failed with:

    qdwin/qdwin.c:48:10: fatal error: libweston/xwayland-api.h: No such file
                         or directory

Adding the header to the libweston install_headers() list restores the devel
surface upstream exposes, rather than diverging from it. The header is a pure
API declaration (function-pointer structs + the two *_get_api accessors); it
pulls in no frontend code and is safe to install regardless of whether the
xwayland module itself is built.

Apply with `patch -p1` from src/.
---
 include/libweston/meson.build | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/libweston/meson.build b/include/libweston/meson.build
--- a/include/libweston/meson.build
+++ b/include/libweston/meson.build
@@ -13,6 +13,14 @@ install_headers(
 	'remoting-plugin.h',
 	'pipewire-plugin.h',
 	'shell-utils.h',
+	# qdistro (J29): upstream installs xwayland-api.h from compositor/, a
+	# subdir this vendored tree deliberately omits (frontend not built), so the
+	# header defined as xwayland_api_h below was never installed. qdwin.c
+	# includes <libweston/xwayland-api.h> unconditionally for
+	# weston_xwayland_surface_get_api() (the is_xwayland toplevel tagging), so
+	# without this the vendored prefix cannot build qdwin. Installing it here
+	# restores upstream's devel surface rather than diverging from it.
+	'xwayland-api.h',
 	subdir: dir_include_libweston_install
 )
 
